      "description": "Staff Dentist (Full-Time) - UT Dentists - UTHealth Houston Bellaire  in Texas, United States | Faculty & Physicians at UTHealth Houston Skip to main content Employee Login External Login Sign up Employee Login External Login Start Your Search UT Physicians Faculty Executive Behavioral Sciences Campus Postdoctoral Research Fellow Internal Applicants Search All Why UTHealth Houston? Benefits Career Development and Recognition Awards & Accolades Join Our Talent Community Veterans Blog Start Your Search UT Physicians Faculty Executive Behavioral Sciences Campus Postdoctoral Research Fellow Internal Applicants Search All Why UTHealth Houston? Benefits Career Development and Recognition Awards & Accolades Join Our Talent Community Veterans Blog Saved jobs (0) - We use cookies to offer you a better browsing experience, analyze site traffic, and personalize content. Read about how we use cookies and how you can control them by visiting our Cookie Settings page. If you continue to use this site, you consent to our use of cookies. Cookie Settings Deny Allow Staff Dentist (Full-Time) - UT Dentists - UTHealth Houston Bellaire Texas Category Faculty & Physicians Job Id 260001OE On-Site Save Apply Now Back to search results Previous job Next job JOB DESCRIPTION UT Dentists – Staff Dentist (Full-Time) – Bellaire UT Dentists , the clinical practice of UTHealth Houston School of Dentistry , is seeking an experienced, clinically accomplished general dentist to help launch and grow a new practice at UTHealth Houston Bellaire Station. This location brings primary care, medical specialty care, and dentistry together in one multidisciplinary setting, creating a rare opportunity to deliver coordinated oral and overall healthcare. Designed to provide a private-practice-caliber patient experience within a leading academic health system, the Bellaire Station practice will emphasize comprehensive care, clinical excellence, personalized service, efficiency, and long-term patient relationships. The dentist will manage a broad patient population, including individuals with complex dental and medical needs, and will collaborate closely with dental specialists, physicians, and other healthcare professionals. This opportunity is intended for a mature clinician with broad-scope general dentistry experience, strong diagnostic and treatment-planning skills, polished communication, and sound clinical judgment. As part of the founding clinical team, the dentist will help establish the practice culture, clinical workflows, service standards, referral relationships, and approach to sustained growth. What we do here changes the world . UTHealth Houston is Texas’s resource for healthcare education, innovation, scientific discovery, and excellence in patient care. That is where you come in. Once you join us, you will not want to leave . It is because we reward our team for the excellent service they provide. Our total rewards package includes the benefits you would expect from a top healthcare organization (benefits, insurance, etc.), plus: 100% paid medical premiums for our full-time employees. Generous time off (holidays, preventative leave day, both vacation and sick time – all of which equates to around 37-38 days per year) Longevity Pay (Monthly payments after two years of service) Build your future with our awesome retirement/pension plan! We take care of our employees! As a world-renowned institution, our employees’ wellbeing is important to us. We offer work/life services such as... Free financial and legal counseling. Free mental health counseling services. Gym membership discounts and access to wellness programs. Other employee discounts include entertainment, car rentals, cell phones, etc. Resources for child and elder care. Plus, many more! Qualifications: Education and Training: Graduation from a CODA-accredited dental school. Completion of a general dentistry residency. Excellent interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills. Preferred: 2+ years of experience. Forward-thinking attitude with a focus on prevention, quality, and value of care, and commitment to working in a public health setting. Fluency in Spanish, Vietnamese, or other foreign language. Licensure and Credentials: Unrestricted license to practice dentistry in the State of Texas. Current CPR (BLS) certification. Valid DEA registration. Skills and Abilities: Comprehensive knowledge of culturally competent, evidence-based, person-centered dental care with a focus on disease prevention, quality, and value for the patient. Appreciation of the impact of the social determinants of health and the capacity to function successfully as part of a large team. Ability to use electronic health records efficiently and proficiently. Apply Now Save If you are looking for a great healthcare career in Houston, visit http://go.uth.edu/careers ! University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston (UTHealth Houston) Established in 1972 by The University of Texas System Board of Regents, The University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston (UTHealth Houston) is Houston’s Health University and Texas’ resource for health care education, innovation, scientific discovery and excellence in patient care. The most comprehensive academic health center in the UT System and the U.S. Gulf Coast region, UTHealth Houston is home to schools of biomedical informatics, biomedical sciences, dentistry, nursing and public health and the John P. and Kathrine G. McGovern Medical School. UTHealth Houston includes The University of Texas Harris County Psychiatric Center, as well as the growing clinical practices UT Physicians, UT Dentists and UT Health Services. The university’s primary teaching hospitals are Memorial Hermann-Texas Medical Center, Children’s Memorial Hermann Hospital and Harris Health Lyndon B. Johnson Hospital. UTHealth Houston Benefits UTHealth Houston offers a comprehensive and competitive benefits package. For more information on our benefits programs please refer to our benefits page . Equal Employment Opportunity Statement UTHealth Houston is committed to providing equal opportunity in all employment-related activities without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), gender, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, or any other basis prohibited by law or University policy. Reasonable accommodation, based on disability or religious observances, will be considered in accordance with applicable law and UTHealth Houston policy. All UTHealth Houston employees who are assigned to work at a location that is subject to the affiliated partner’s hospital, clinical offices, or agency are required to abide by UTHealth Houston’s rules and regulations, as well as the affiliate’s rules and regulations. In accordance with Executive Order GA-48 and to the extent that this position requires you to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Texas Business and Commerce Code §117.001(2), this role will include routine reviews to determine whether things such as criminal history or continuous connections to the government or political apparatus of a foreign adversary might prevent you from being able to maintain the security or integrity of the infrastructure. A foreign adversary is a nation listed in 15 C.F.R. §791.4. Share this job Share via LinkedIn Share via Facebook Share via twitter Share via email Share job link To your colleagues or friends Cancel Copy Link Get notified for similar jobs You'll receive updates once a week Enter Email address (Required) Activate Manage alerts Failure! Ok Get tailored job\n                                recommendations based on your interests. Get Started profile icon 4 hours. Sign up Profile recommendations See all jobs See less jobs See all jobs See even more No recommendations found Similar Jobs Staff Dentists