      "title": "Staff Physician Optometrist",
      "description": "Staff Physician Optometrist - Ophthalmology, McGovern Medical School in Texas, United States | Faculty & Physicians at UTHealth Houston Skip to main content Employee Login External Login Sign up Employee Login External Login Start Your Search UT Physicians Faculty Executive Behavioral Sciences Campus Postdoctoral Research Fellow Internal Applicants Search All Why UTHealth Houston? Benefits Career Development and Recognition Awards & Accolades Join Our Talent Community Veterans Blog Start Your Search UT Physicians Faculty Executive Behavioral Sciences Campus Postdoctoral Research Fellow Internal Applicants Search All Why UTHealth Houston? Benefits Career Development and Recognition Awards & Accolades Join Our Talent Community Veterans Blog Saved jobs (0) - We use cookies to offer you a better browsing experience, analyze site traffic, and personalize content. Read about how we use cookies and how you can control them by visiting our Cookie Settings page. If you continue to use this site, you consent to our use of cookies. Cookie Settings Deny Allow Staff Physician Optometrist - Ophthalmology, McGovern Medical School Texas Category Faculty & Physicians Job Id 2600006A On-Site Save Apply Now Back to search results Previous job Next job JOB DESCRIPTION The Ruiz Department of Ophthalmology and Visual Science , McGovern Medical School at UTHealth Houston , seeks an optometrist to join its faculty. UTHealth Houston offers a dynamic academic environment, competitive compensation, and comprehensive benefits. Position Key Accountabilities: The Ruiz Department of Ophthalmology and Visual Science seeks an optometrist to join our expanding clinical practice. Responsibilities may include patient medical management, refractive care, and same-day appointment screening and triage, based on the candidate's experience and interests. Practice locations may include the Texas Medical Center and the planned Bellaire Station location, expected to open in 2027. As services expand, opportunities may arise to participate in additional clinical or administrative activities. Qualifications: The selected candidate must have a degree in optometry and a Texas Medical License or be eligible for a Texas Temporary License. Candidates with experience or an interest in refractive surgery are encouraged to apply, though this is not required. This is a staff position with the potential to transition to an academic appointment based on demonstrated academic contributions and potential. Apply Now Save If you are looking for a great healthcare career in Houston, visit http://go.uth.edu/careers ! University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston (UTHealth Houston) Established in 1972 by The University of Texas System Board of Regents, The University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston (UTHealth Houston) is Houston’s Health University and Texas’ resource for health care education, innovation, scientific discovery and excellence in patient care. The most comprehensive academic health center in the UT System and the U.S. Gulf Coast region, UTHealth Houston is home to schools of biomedical informatics, biomedical sciences, dentistry, nursing and public health and the John P. and Kathrine G. McGovern Medical School. UTHealth Houston includes The University of Texas Harris County Psychiatric Center, as well as the growing clinical practices UT Physicians, UT Dentists and UT Health Services. The university’s primary teaching hospitals are Memorial Hermann-Texas Medical Center, Children’s Memorial Hermann Hospital and Harris Health Lyndon B. Johnson Hospital. UTHealth Houston Benefits UTHealth Houston offers a comprehensive and competitive benefits package. For more information on our benefits programs please refer to our benefits page . Equal Employment Opportunity Statement UTHealth Houston is committed to providing equal opportunity in all employment-related activities without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbir