    "https://careers.uth.tmc.edu/us/en/job/260001U8/Staff-Physician-Interventional-Radiologist-Community-Division-Diagnostic-and-Interventional-Imaging-McGovern-Medical-School": {
      "title": "Staff Physician, Interventional Radiologist (Community Division)",
      "description": "Staff Physician, Interventional Radiologist (Community Division) - Diagnostic and Interventional Imaging, McGovern Medical School in Texas Medical Center-Houston, Texas, United States | Faculty & Physicians at UTHealth Houston Skip to main content Employee Login External Login Sign up Employee Login External Login Start Your Search UT Physicians Faculty Executive Behavioral Sciences Campus Postdoctoral Research Fellow Internal Applicants Search All Why UTHealth Houston? Benefits Career Development and Recognition Awards & Accolades Join Our Talent Community Veterans Blog Start Your Search UT Physicians Faculty Executive Behavioral Sciences Campus Postdoctoral Research Fellow Internal Applicants Search All Why UTHealth Houston? Benefits Career Development and Recognition Awards & Accolades Join Our Talent Community Veterans Blog Saved jobs (0) - We use cookies to offer you a better browsing experience, analyze site traffic, and personalize content. Read about how we use cookies and how you can control them by visiting our Cookie Settings page. If you continue to use this site, you consent to our use of cookies. Cookie Settings Deny Allow Staff Physician, Interventional Radiologist (Community Division) - Diagnostic and Interventional Imaging, McGovern Medical School Texas Medical Center-Houston, Texas Category Faculty & Physicians Job Id 260001U8 On-Site Save Apply Now Back to search results Previous job Next job JOB DESCRIPTION The Department of Diagnostic & Interventional Imaging is seeking a trained Interventional Radiologist to join our growing radiology department across the Greater Houston area. The successful candidate will provide a broad range of image-guided diagnostic procedures. Position Key Accountabilities: Perform a broad range of image-guided minimally invasive procedures. Evaluate patients in consultation and determine appropriate interventional treatment. Perform vascular and nonvascular interventions, including biopsies, drainages, vascular access, embolization procedures, and other procedures appropriate to the physician's expertise. Participate in inpatient and outpatient interventional radiology services. Collaborate with referring physicians and multidisciplinary care teams. Provide pre- and post-procedure patient management. Participate in departmental quality improvement, education, and peer-review activities. Participate in call coverage as assigned. Qualifications: MD or DO degree from an accredited medical school. Completion of an accredited Diagnostic Radiology residency. Fellowship training in Interventional Radiology or equivalent qualifications. Board certification or board eligibility in Interventional Radiology/Diagnostic Radiology. Texas Medical License or Faculty Temporary License. Strong clinical, procedural, communication, and interpersonal skills. Experience with a broad range of vascular and nonvascular interventions. Commitment to high-quality, patient-centered care. Apply Now Save If you are looking for a great healthcare career in Houston, visit http://go.uth.edu/careers ! University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston (UTHealth Houston) Established in 1972 by The University of Texas System Board of Regents, The University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston (UTHealth Houston) is Houston’s Health University and Texas’ resource for health care education, innovation, scientific discovery and excellence in patient care. The most comprehensive academic health center in the UT System and the U.S. Gulf Coast region, UTHealth Houston is home to schools of biomedical informatics, biomedical sciences, dentistry, nursing and public health and the John P. and Kathrine G. McGovern Medical School. UTHealth Houston includes The University of Texas Harris County Psychiatric Center, as well as the growing clinical practices UT Physicians, UT Dentists and UT Health Services. The university’s primary teaching hospitals are Memorial Hermann-Texas Medical Center, Children’