      "title": "Faculty (Open Rank)",
      "description": "Faculty (Open Rank) - Dermatology, McGovern Medical School  in Texas Medical Center-Houston, Texas, United States | Faculty & Physicians at UTHealth Houston Skip to main content Employee Login External Login Employee Login External Login Start Your Search UT Physicians Faculty Executive Behavioral Sciences Campus Postdoctoral Research Fellow Internal Applicants Search All Why UTHealth Houston? Benefits Career Development and Recognition Awards & Accolades Join Our Talent Community Veterans Blog Start Your Search UT Physicians Faculty Executive Behavioral Sciences Campus Postdoctoral Research Fellow Internal Applicants Search All Why UTHealth Houston? Benefits Career Development and Recognition Awards & Accolades Join Our Talent Community Veterans Blog Saved jobs (0) - We use cookies to offer you a better browsing experience, analyze site traffic, and personalize content. Read about how we use cookies and how you can control them by visiting our Cookie Settings page. If you continue to use this site, you consent to our use of cookies. Cookie Settings Deny Allow Faculty (Open Rank) - Dermatology, McGovern Medical School Texas Medical Center-Houston, Texas Category Faculty & Physicians Job Id 2600016K On-Site Save Apply Now Back to search results Previous job Next job JOB DESCRIPTION McGovern Medical School at UTHealth Houston seeks faculty at the Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor ranks in the Department of Dermatology . UTHealth Houston is the most comprehensive academic health center in the UT System and the U.S. Gulf Coast region. We are proud to be part of the world’s largest medical center, which enables us to partner with several nationally recognized clinical affiliates.  The university's primary teaching hospitals are Memorial Hermann-Texas Medical Center (TMC) , Children's Memorial Hermann Hospital , and Harris Health Lyndon B. Johnson Hospital . The Department of Dermatology provides exceptional dermatologic care across six+ locations, including UT Physicians Bellaire Station and Harris Health clinics, with strong interdepartmental collaboration and UT MD Anderson, and expertise in adult and pediatric dermatology, surgical dermatology, dermatopathology, and cosmetic treatments. Position Key Accountabilities: Areas of subspecialty interest may include inpatient consultative dermatology, complex medical dermatology, and/or dermatology of skin of color. The successful candidate will provide patient care and participate in the training of our residents and students. Qualifications: MD Board-certified or board-eligible in Dermatology The ideal candidate will have a strong interest in both practicing and teaching general dermatology. A commitment to resident education is necessary. Apply Now Save If you are looking for a great healthcare career in Houston, visit http://go.uth.edu/careers ! University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston (UTHealth Houston) Established in 1972 by The University of Texas System Board of Regents, The University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston (UTHealth Houston) is Houston’s Health University and Texas’ resource for health care education, innovation, scientific discovery and excellence in patient care. The most comprehensive academic health center in the UT System and the U.S. Gulf Coast region, UTHealth Houston is home to schools of biomedical informatics, biomedical sciences, dentistry, nursing and public health and the John P. and Kathrine G. McGovern Medical School. UTHealth Houston includes The University of Texas Harris County Psychiatric Center, as well as the growing clinical practices UT Physicians, UT Dentists and UT Health Services. The university’s primary teaching hospitals are Memorial Hermann-Texas Medical Center, Children’s Memorial Hermann Hospital and Harris Health Lyndon B. Johnson Hospital. UTHealth Houston Benefits UTHealth Houston offers a comprehensive and competitive benefits package. For more information on our benefits programs please refer to our benefits page . Equal Employment Opportunity Statement UTHealth Houston is committed to providing equal opportunity in all employment-related activities without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), gender, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, or any other basis prohibited by law or University policy. Reasonable accommodation, based on disability or religious observances, will be considered in accordance with applicable law and UTHealth Houston policy. All UTHealth Houston employees who are assigned to work at a location that is subject to the affiliated partner’s hospital, clinical offices, or agency are required to abide by UTHealth Houston’s rules and regulations, as well as the affiliate’s rules and regulations. In accordance with Executive Order GA-48 and to the extent that this position requires you to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Texas Business and Commerce Code §117.001(2), this role will include routine reviews to determine whether things such as criminal history or continuous connections to the government or political apparatus of a foreign adversary might prevent you from being able to maintain the security or integrity of the infrastructure. A foreign adversary is a nation listed in 15 C.F.R. §791.4. Share this job Share via LinkedIn Share via Facebook Share via twitter Share via email Share job link To your colleagues or friends Cancel Copy Link Get notified for similar jobs You'll receive updates once a week Enter Email address (Required) Activate Manage alerts Failure! Ok Get tailored job\n                                recommendations based on your interests. Get Started profile icon 4 hours. Sign up Profile recommendations See all jobs See less jobs See all jobs See even more No recommendations found Similar Jobs Faculty (Open Rank) - De