    "https://careers.uth.tmc.edu/us/en/job/260001ZT/Faculty-Open-Rank-Neurocognitive-Neurology-McGovern-Medical-School": {
      "title": "Faculty (Open Rank)",
      "description": "Faculty (Open Rank) | Neurocognitive - Neurology, McGovern Medical School in Texas Medical Center-Houston, Texas, United States | Faculty & Physicians at UTHealth Houston Skip to main content Employee Login External Login Sign up Employee Login External Login Start Your Search UT Physicians Faculty Executive Behavioral Sciences Campus Postdoctoral Research Fellow Internal Applicants Search All Why UTHealth Houston? Benefits Career Development and Recognition Awards & Accolades Join Our Talent Community Veterans Blog Start Your Search UT Physicians Faculty Executive Behavioral Sciences Campus Postdoctoral Research Fellow Internal Applicants Search All Why UTHealth Houston? Benefits Career Development and Recognition Awards & Accolades Join Our Talent Community Veterans Blog Saved jobs (0) - We use cookies to offer you a better browsing experience, analyze site traffic, and personalize content. Read about how we use cookies and how you can control them by visiting our Cookie Settings page. If you continue to use this site, you consent to our use of cookies. Cookie Settings Deny Allow Faculty (Open Rank) | Neurocognitive - Neurology, McGovern Medical School Texas Medical Center-Houston, Texas Category Faculty & Physicians Job Id 260001ZT On-Site Save Apply Now Back to search results Previous job Next job JOB DESCRIPTION The Department of Neurology at McGovern Medical School at UTHealth Houston is seeking an outstanding faculty physician to join the Division of Dementia and Memory Disorders at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor , commensurate with academic accomplishments and experience. McGovern Medical School at UTHealth Houston is committed to advancing innovative patient care, education, and discovery. We invite applications from neurologists passionate about improving the lives of patients and families affected by dementia and other neurodegenerative disorders and eager to contribute to a dynamic, collaborative academic environment. Our ideal candidate brings expertise or a strong interest in cognitive neurology, dementia, and memory disorders , with particular enthusiasm for clinical trials, translational research, neurodegenerative movement disorders, and the psychiatric manifestations of neurodegenerative disease . This is an exciting opportunity to join a growing academic program and contribute to the division's missions of clinical excellence, discovery, education, and service . The successful candidate will have the opportunity to develop and expand their clinical and academic interests while collaborating with multidisciplinary colleagues across UTHealth Houston. Position Highlights: Clinical practice focused on dementia, memory disorders, and cognitive neurology. Opportunities to participate in and develop clinical trials and translational research . Opportunities for collaboration in neurodegenerative movement disorders and neuropsychiatric manifestations of neurodegenerative disease. Participation in the education and mentorship of medical students, residents, fellows, and other learners. Opportunity to contribute to the growth and academic mission of a leading medical school and health sciences center. Qualifications: Medical degree (MD or DO) from an accredited medical school. Completion of an ACGME-accredited neurology residency. Completion of an ACGME-accredited fellowship in dementia, memory disorders, or cognitive neurology ABPN board certification or eligibility in Neurology Texas medical license or eligibility for Texas licensure. Excellent clinical skills, including comprehensive history-taking, neurological examination, and interpretation of diagnostic studies. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to effectively communicate with patients, families, trainees, and interdisciplinary team members. Demonstrated commitment to compassionate, patient-centered care. Ability to work collaboratively in a team-oriented academic environment. Commitment to excellence, discovery, education, and service, with the potential to be outstanding in one's area of expertise. Candidates with a demonstrated record of clinical excellence, scholarly activity, research, clinical trials, translational investigation, and academic leadership are particularly encouraged to apply. Join us in advancing the future of dementia and memory disorders care, research, and education at McGovern Medical School. Apply Now Save If you are looking for a great healthcare career in Houston, visit http://go.uth.edu/careers ! University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston (UTHealth Houston) Established in 1972 by The University of Texas System Board of Regents, The University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston (UTHealth Houston) is Houston’s Health University and Texas’ resource for health care education, innovation, scientific discovery and excellence in patient care. The most comprehensive academic health center in the UT System and the U.S. Gulf Coast region, UTHealth Houston is home to schools of biomedical informatics, biomedical sciences, dentistry, nursing and public health and the John P. and Kathrine G. McGovern Medical School. UTHealth Houston includes The University of Texas Harris County Psychiatric Center, as well as the growing clinical practices UT Physicians, UT Dentists and UT Health Services. The university’s primary teaching hospitals are Memorial Hermann-Texas Medical Center, Children’s Memorial Hermann Hospital and Harris Health Lyndon B. Johnson Hospital. UTHealth Houston Benefits UTHealth Houston offers a comprehensive and competitive benefits package. For more information on our benefits programs please refer to our benefits page . Equal Employment Opportunity Statement UTHealth Houston is committed to providing equal opportunity in all employment-related activities without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), gender, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, or any other basis prohibited by law or University policy. Reasonable accommodation, based on disability or religious observances, will be considered in accordance with applicable law and UTHealth Houston policy. All UTHealth Houston employees who are assigned to work at a location that is subject to the affiliated partner’s hospital, clinical offices, or agency are required to abide by UTHealth Houston’s rules and regulations, as well as the affiliate’s rules and regulations. In accordance with Executive Order GA-48 and to the extent that this position requires you to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Texas Business and Commerce Code §117.001(2), this role will include routine reviews to determine whether things such as criminal history or continuous connections to the government or political apparatus of a foreign adversary might prevent you from being able to maintain the security or integrity of the infrastructure. A foreign adversary is a nation listed in 15 C.F.R. §791.4. Share this job Share via LinkedIn Share via Facebook Share via twitter Share via email Share job link To your colleagues or friends Cancel Copy Link Get notified for similar jobs You'll receive updates once a week Enter Email address (Required) Activate Manage alerts Failure! Ok Get tailored job\n                                recommendations based on your interests. Get Started profile icon 4 hours. Sign up Profile recommendations See all jobs See less jobs See all jobs See even more No recommendations found Similar Jobs Faculty (Open Rank) Neuromuscular - Neurology, McGovern Medical School Location Texas, United States Category Faculty & Physicians Posted Date 10/21/2026 Faculty (Open Rank), Headache - Neurology, McGovern Medical School Location Texas Medical Center-Houston, Texas, United States Category Faculty & Physicians Posted Date 10/21/2026 Faculty (Open Rank),