    "https://careers.uth.tmc.edu/us/en/job/2600024C/Staff-Physician-Casual-Nuclear-Medicine-Diagnostic-and-Interventional-Imaging-McGovern-Medical-School": {
      "title": "Staff Physician (Casual), Nuclear Medicine",
      "description": "Staff Physician (Casual), Nuclear Medicine - Diagnostic and Interventional Imaging, McGovern Medical School in Texas Medical Center-Houston, Texas, United States | Faculty & Physicians at UTHealth Houston Skip to main content Employee Login External Login Sign up Employee Login External Login Start Your Search UT Physicians Faculty Executive Behavioral Sciences Campus Postdoctoral Research Fellow Internal Applicants Search All Why UTHealth Houston? Benefits Career Development and Recognition Awards & Accolades Join Our Talent Community Veterans Blog Start Your Search UT Physicians Faculty Executive Behavioral Sciences Campus Postdoctoral Research Fellow Internal Applicants Search All Why UTHealth Houston? Benefits Career Development and Recognition Awards & Accolades Join Our Talent Community Veterans Blog Saved jobs (0) - We use cookies to offer you a better browsing experience, analyze site traffic, and personalize content. Read about how we use cookies and how you can control them by visiting our Cookie Settings page. If you continue to use this site, you consent to our use of cookies. Cookie Settings Deny Allow Staff Physician (Casual), Nuclear Medicine - Diagnostic and Interventional Imaging, McGovern Medical School Texas Medical Center-Houston, Texas Category Faculty & Physicians Job Id 2600024C On-Site Save Apply Now Back to search results Previous job Next job JOB DESCRIPTION The Department of Diagnostic & Interventional Imaging is seeking a trained Staff Physician in Nuclear Medicine to join our growing radiology department across the Greater Houston area. The successful candidate will provide a broad range of image-guided diagnostic procedures. Position Key Accountabilities: Perform and interpret a broad range of nuclear medicine and molecular imaging studies, including PET/CT, SPECT/CT, planar imaging, and other specialized examinations. Evaluate patients and determine the most appropriate nuclear medicine imaging or therapeutic approach. Provide and oversee radiopharmaceutical therapies in accordance with established clinical protocols and regulatory requirements. Collaborate with referring physicians and multidisciplinary care teams to support accurate diagnosis, treatment planning, and follow-up. Provide pre- and post-procedure patient management, including counseling regarding preparation, radiation safety, and follow-up care. Participate in inpatient and outpatient nuclear medicine services across affiliated clinical sites. Contribute to departmental quality improvement, education, research, and peer-review activities. Participate in resident, fellow, technologist, and medical student education. Participate in call coverage as assigned. Qualifications: MD or DO degree from an accredited medical school. Completion of an accredited Diagnostic Radiology residency or equivalent training. Fellowship training in Nuclear Medicine, Nuclear Radiology, or equivalent qualifications. Board certification or board eligibility in Diagnostic Radiology and/or Nuclear Medicine, as applicable. Texas Medical License or Faculty Temporary License. Eligibility for appropriate federal and state radioactive materials and radiopharmaceutical authorizations. Strong clinical, interpretive, communication, and interpersonal skills. Experience with PET/CT, SPECT/CT, radionuclide therapy, and other nuclear medicine procedures preferred. Commitment to patient-centered care, multidisciplinary collaboration, education, and continuous quality improvement. Apply Now Save If you are looking for a great healthcare career in Houston, visit http://go.uth.edu/careers ! University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston (UTHealth Houston) Established in 1972 by The University of Texas System Board of Regents, The University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston (UTHealth Houston) is Houston’s Health University and Texas’ resource for health care education, innovation, scientific discovery and excellence in patient care. The most comprehensive academic health center in the UT System and the U.S. Gulf Coast region, UTHealth Houston is home to schools of biomedical informatics, biomedical sciences, dentistry, nursing and public health and the John P. and Kathrine G. McGovern Medical School. UTHealth Houston includes The University of Texas Harris County Psychiatric Center, as well as the growing clinical practices UT Physicians, UT Dentists and UT Health Services. The university’s primary teaching hospitals are Memorial Hermann-Texas Medical Center, Children’s Memorial Hermann Hospital and Harris Health Lyndon B. Johnson Hospital. UTHealth Houston Benefits UTHealth Houston offers a comprehensive and competitive benefits package. For more information on our benefits programs please refer to our benefits page . Equal Employment Opportunity Statement UTHealth Houston is committed to providing equal opportunity in all employment-related activities without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), gender, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, or any other basis prohibited by law or University policy. Reasonable accommodation, based on disability or religious observances, will be considered in accordance with applicable law and UTHealth Houston policy. All UTHealth Houston employees who are assigned to work at a location that is subject to the affiliated partner’s hospital, clinical offices, or agency are required to abide by UTHealth Houston’s rules and regulations, as well as the affiliate’s rules and regulations. In accordance with Executive Order GA-48 and to the extent that this position requires you to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Texas Business and Commerce Code §117.001(2), this role will include routine reviews to determine whether things such as criminal history or continuous connections to the gov