    "https://careers.uth.tmc.edu/us/en/job/2600011O/Faculty-Open-Rank-Outpatient-Neurology-MHH-Southwest-McGovern-Medical-School": {
      "title": "Faculty (Open Rank) Outpatient Neurology, MHH Southwest",
      "description": "Faculty (Open Rank) Outpatient Neurology, MHH Southwest - McGovern Medical School in Houston, Texas, United States | Faculty & Physicians at UTHealth Houston Skip to main content Employee Login External Login Sign up Employee Login External Login Start Your Search UT Physicians Faculty Executive Behavioral Sciences Campus Postdoctoral Research Fellow Internal Applicants Search All Why UTHealth Houston? Benefits Career Development and Recognition Awards & Accolades Join Our Talent Community Veterans Blog Start Your Search UT Physicians Faculty Executive Behavioral Sciences Campus Postdoctoral Research Fellow Internal Applicants Search All Why UTHealth Houston? Benefits Career Development and Recognition Awards & Accolades Join Our Talent Community Veterans Blog Saved jobs (0) - We use cookies to offer you a better browsing experience, analyze site traffic, and personalize content. Read about how we use cookies and how you can control them by visiting our Cookie Settings page. If you continue to use this site, you consent to our use of cookies. Cookie Settings Deny Allow Faculty (Open Rank) Outpatient Neurology, MHH Southwest - McGovern Medical School Houston, Texas Category Faculty & Physicians Job Id 2600011O On-Site Save Apply Now Back to search results Previous job Next job JOB DESCRIPTION McGovern Medical School at UTHealth Houston , Department of Neurology , is seeking a full-time Board-Certified or Board-Eligible General Neurologist to join an outpatient practice at Memorial Hermann Southwest Hospital . This position is designed for an experienced, highly efficient clinician who is comfortable managing a high-volume ambulatory practice while delivering excellent patient care. The role is primarily outpatient. No inpatient coverage is required. Limited inpatient responsibilities are available if desired, but would make up a small portion of the role. Position Key Accountabilities : · Provide comprehensive outpatient neurology care for adult patients with a broad range of neurologic conditions, including headache, epilepsy, movement disorders, peripheral neuropathy, multiple sclerosis, and cognitive disorders. · Manage a high-volume clinic with a focus on efficiency, access, and continuity of care. · Perform office-based procedures, including EMG and botulinum toxin injections, as appropriate. · Coordinate care with primary care physicians and other specialists to support optimal patient outcomes. · Ensure accurate and timely documentation and appropriate coding. · Participate in a shared outpatient call pool for non-urgent clinical issues, with coverage limited to several weeks per year. · Maintain clinical productivity consistent with a high-performing outpatient neurology practice. · Participate in the education of medical students, neurology residents, and, when applicable, neurophysiology fellows. · Contribute to departmental clinical operations and quality efforts as needed. · Attendance at weekly Neurology Grand Rounds and monthly Neurology faculty meetings (virtual option is provided) Compensation and Productivity : Compensation includes a competitive salary and an RVU-based model aligned with high clinical productivity, typically ranging from 9,000 to 10,000 RVUs annually, and commensurate with experience. Qualifications: · MD or DO degree from an accredited medical school · Completion of an ACGME-accredited Neurology residency · Board Certified or Board Eligible in Neurology · Eligible for holding an unrestricted Texas Medical license · Eligible for hospital privileges at affiliated facilities Apply Now Save If you are looking for a great healthcare career in Houston, visit http://go.uth.edu/careers ! University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston (UTHealth Houston) Established in 1972 by The University of Texas System Board of Regents, The University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston (UTHealth Houston) is Houston’s Health University and Texas’ resource for health care education, innovation, scientific discovery and excellence in patient care. The most comprehensive academic health center in the UT System and the U.S. Gulf Coast region, UTHealth Houston is home to schools of biomedical informatics, biomedical sciences, dentistry, nursing and public health and the John P. and Kathrine G. McGovern Medical School. UTHealth Houston includes The University of Texas Harris County Psychiatric Center, as well as the growing clinical practices UT Physicians, UT Dentists and UT Health Services. The university’s primary teaching hospitals are Memorial Hermann-Texas Medical Center, Children’s Memorial Hermann Hospital and Harris Health Lyndon B. Johnson Hospital. UTHealth Houston Benefits UTHealth Houston offers a comprehensive and competitive benefits package. For more information on our benefits programs please refer to our benefits page . Equal Employment Opportunity Statement UTHealth Houston is committed to providing equal opportunity in all employment-related activities without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), gender, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, or any other basis prohibited by law or University policy. Reasonable accommodation, based on disability or religious observances, will be considered in accordance with applicable law and UTHealth Houston policy. All UTHealth Houston employees who are assigned to work at a location that is subject to the affiliated partner’s hospital, clinical offices, or agency are required to abide by UTHealth Houston’s rules and regulations, as well as the affiliate’s rules and regulations. In accordance with Executive Order GA-48 and to the extent that this position requires you to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Texas Business and Commerce Code §117.001(2), this role will include routine reviews to determine whether things such as criminal history or continuous connections to the government or political apparatus of a foreign adversary might prevent you from being able to maintain the security or integrity of the infrastructure. A foreign adversary is a nation listed in 15 C.F.R. §791.4. Share this job Share via LinkedIn Share via Facebook Share via twitter Share via email Share job link To your colleagues or friends Cancel Copy Link Get notified for similar jobs You'll receive updates once a week Enter Email address (Required) Activate Manage alerts Failure! Ok Get tailored job\n                                recommendations based on your interests. Get Started profile icon 4 hours. Sign up Profile recommendations See all jobs See less jobs See all jobs See even more No recommendations found Similar Jobs Faculty (Open Rank), Headache - Neurology, McGovern Medical School Location Texas Medical Center-Houston, Texas, United States Category Faculty & Physicians Posted Date 10/21/2026 Faculty (Open Rank) Neuromuscular - Neurology, McGovern Medical School Location Texas, United States Category Faculty & Physicians Posted Date 10/21/2026 Faculty (Open Rank) | Neurocognitive - Neurology, McGovern Medical School Location Texas Medical Center-Houston, Texas, United States Category Faculty & Physicians Posted Date 10/21/2026 Faculty (Open Rank) - Dermatology, McGovern Medical School Location Texas Medical Center-Houston, Texas, United States Category Faculty & Physicians Posted Date 10/21/2026 Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor, Pediatric CV- Anesthesiology, McGovern Medical School Location Texas, United States Category Faculty & Physicians Posted Date 10/21/2026 Vice Chair of Clinical Operations, Faculty (Open Rank) – Neurology, McGovern Medical School Location Texas Medical Center-Houston, Texas, United States Category Faculty & Physicians Posted Date 10/21/2026 Faculty (Open Rank), General Inpatient and Vascular Neurology Inpatient and Telemedicine, McGovern Medical School Location Texas Medical Center-Houston, Texas, United States Category Faculty & Physicians Posted Date 10/21/2026 Staff Physician (Casual), Nuclear Medicine - Diagnostic and Interventional Imaging, McGovern Medical School Location Texas Medical Center-Houston, Texas, United States Category Faculty & Physicians Posted Date 10/21/2026 Faculty (Open Rank) | Division Chief, Epilepsy - Neurology, McGovern Medical Center Location Texas Medical Center-Houston, Texas, United States Category Faculty & Physicians Posted Date 10/21/2026 See more See less See next See even more No recommendations found Jobseekers Also Viewed See more See less See next See even more No recommendations found Career Site Cookie Settings Personal Information 7000 Fannin Street Houston, Texas 77030 ​​​​​​​ 713-500-4HSC ​​​​​​​713-500-4472 Resources Open Records Site Policies Institutional Resume HUB Program Report Sexual Misconduct follow us Copyright © 2023 UTHealth Houston Blog 04525f084cbc4481a03c38a5a17331a3 > ] Artboard Created with Sketch. 512/Filter Career Bot Conversational Bot Enabled Chatbot Sounds The information you provide to the chatbot will be collected to improve your experience. Please read our privacy policy to see how we are storing and protecting your data Today 05:21 pm Bot message Hi There! Are you interested in this job? I'm interested Similar Jobs Chatbot User Input box with Send button"
