    "https://careers.uth.tmc.edu/us/en/job/260000KG/Psychologist-Outpatient-Memorial-Hermann-Pediatric-Specialty-Outpatient-Clinic-at-Katy-Louis-A-Faillace-MD-Department-of-Psychiatry-Behavioral-Sciences": {
      "title": "Psychologist- Outpatient/ Memorial Hermann Pediatric Specialty Outpatient Clinic",
      "description": "Psychologist- Outpatient/ Memorial Hermann Pediatric Specialty Outpatient Clinic at Katy - Louis A. Faillace, MD., Department of Psychiatry & Behavioral Sciences in Texas, United States | Faculty & Physicians at UTHealth Houston Skip to main content Employee Login External Login Sign up Employee Login External Login Start Your Search UT Physicians Faculty Executive Behavioral Sciences Campus Postdoctoral Research Fellow Internal Applicants Search All Why UTHealth Houston? Benefits Career Development and Recognition Awards & Accolades Join Our Talent Community Veterans Blog Start Your Search UT Physicians Faculty Executive Behavioral Sciences Campus Postdoctoral Research Fellow Internal Applicants Search All Why UTHealth Houston? Benefits Career Development and Recognition Awards & Accolades Join Our Talent Community Veterans Blog Saved jobs (0) - We use cookies to offer you a better browsing experience, analyze site traffic, and personalize content. Read about how we use cookies and how you can control them by visiting our Cookie Settings page. If you continue to use this site, you consent to our use of cookies. Cookie Settings Deny Allow Psychologist- Outpatient/ Memorial Hermann Pediatric Specialty Outpatient Clinic at Katy - Louis A. Faillace, MD., Department of Psychiatry & Behavioral Sciences Texas Category Faculty & Physicians Job Id 260000KG On-Site Apply Now Back to search results Previous job Next job JOB DESCRIPTION The Department of Psychiatry and Behavioral Sciences of McGovern Medical School at UTHealth Houston is seeking qualified candidates to join its outstanding faculty. This position offers the opportunity to work on a state-of-the-art Behavioral Sciences Campus that includes two psychiatric hospitals with a combined capacity of 500 beds and 29 outpatient clinics across the greater Houston area. Located in the heart of the nation’s largest medical center, the department supports a robust research enterprise and a wide range of educational programs, including a large psychiatry residency, a child and adolescent fellowship, psychology internship training, and additional advanced programs. Our collaborative and collegial environment promotes interdisciplinary teamwork. The selected candidate will play a key role in teaching and clinical supervision of psychology predoctoral interns, postdoctoral fellows, practicum students, and psychiatry residents and fellows, serving as a core training site for McGovern Medical School and the new School of Behavioral Health Sciences. Position Key Accountabilities: The selected faculty member will serve as a Clinical Psychologist in the Department of Psychiatry and Behavioral Sciences, with assignment to the Memorial Hermann Pediatric Specialty Outpatient Clinic at Katy. Responsibilities include conducting psychological assessments and consultations, developing treatment plans, and providing evidence-based individual, family, and group therapy. The position also contributes to the department’s missions in education, research, and patient care. Qualifications: Psy.D. or Ph.D. in clinical or counseling psychology from an APA-accredited program Licensed or eligible for license by the Texas State Board of Examiners of Psychologists Apply Now If you are looking for a great healthcare career in Houston, visit http://go.uth.edu/careers ! University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston (UTHealth Houston) Established in 1972 by The University of Texas System Board of Regents, The University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston (UTHealth Houston) is Houston’s Health University and Texas’ resource for health care education, innovation, scientific discovery and excellence in patient care. The most comprehensive academic health center in the UT System and the U.S. Gulf Coast region, UTHealth Houston is home to schools of biomedical informatics, biomedical sciences, dentistry, nursing and public health and the John P. and Kathrine G. McGovern Medical School. U